DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 1 Advance concept.

Advanced Linux Concepts (0–2 Years Experience)

After learning basic Linux commands, interviewers quickly move to real-world Linux scenarios.
These questions test whether you can handle production systems, not just run commands.

 Tool 1 Advance concept Focus: Advanced Linux Interview Questions

• What happens when a Linux system boots?
• Explain the Linux booting process step by step
• What is systemd and why is it important?
• Difference between systemctl and service
• How do you start, stop, restart, and enable a service?
• What are runlevels and targets?
• What is a zombie process?
• How do you find and troubleshoot high CPU or memory usage?
• Difference between load average and CPU utilization
• What is swap memory? When is it used?
• How do you analyze disk space issues on a server?
• How do you check inode usage?
• What is log rotation? Why is it needed?
• Explain logrotate
• Where are system logs stored in Linux?
• Difference between /var/log/messages and /var/log/syslog
• How do you check application logs?
• What is crontab? Give a real-world example
• Difference between cron and at
• How do you monitor Linux server health?

💡 Real Interview Insight:
Interviewers often ask:
👉 “A production server is slow — how will you troubleshoot?”
If you can confidently answer Linux troubleshooting steps, you already stand out.
